Miss Amanda Taylor, a 72-year-old African American female, presents for a follow-up visit. She has a history of alcohol use disorder and mild hypercholesterolemia. At her last visit on April 16th, her blood pressure was 130/90 mmHg. Today, she presented with a reading of 150/100 mmHg. She was previously prescribed hydrochlorothiazide 12.5 mg PO QD and lisinopril 20 mg PO QD. She reports struggling with alcohol cessation and was advised on the potential benefits of stopping alcohol consumption. She admits to drinking 4-5 days per week and is willing to try the injectable form of naltrexone to assist with her alcohol cravings.

**Review of Systems (ROS):**
