**1. Subjective:**

**Chief Complaint (CC):**
Right shoulder pain.

**History of Present Illness (HPI):**
Matthew Smith is a 67-year-old male who presents to the urgent care center for an evaluation of right shoulder pain. The patient reports that the pain began approximately 4 days ago after he was tackled during a game of tackle football. He describes the pain as moderate and notes that it has been persistent since the incident. The patient mentions that the pain is constant and has been affecting his ability to perform overhead activities and lift objects. He also reports a mild headache and slight discomfort when putting his hand on his head. He has been taking a small amount of Tylenol for the pain but finds it only minimally effective. Matthew has been active in recreational sports, particularly tackle football, for most of his life and has recently started playing again. He is anxious to return to the sport but is concerned about the injury.

